      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s only parish, Saint Donatus Church, is the only U.S. church named for the storm‑protecting saint.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://digitalcollections.loras.edu/items/show/6283",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Every Holy Week, pilgrims walk a half‑mile path behind the church, stopping at fourteen stations of the Cross.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://iowaroadtrip.net/st-donatus/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The original stone church, built in the 19th century, survived a fire and remains a historic landmark.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
